       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). That is double the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg per dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. It raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day total)\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
